<div class="page">
  <header style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">2012 Western U.S. Wildland Fires</h1>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin: 0;">Julie Winchester, Cooperative Institute for Research in the Atmosphere, Colorado State University, Ft. Collins, CO</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin: 0;">IMPROVE</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 2;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Historical Wildfire Trends</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">The National Interagency Fire Center 2012 report stated that lower than average precipitation and warmer temperatures contributed to a significant increase in the number and size of wildfires across the Western United States. The report also noted that the increasing frequency and intensity of these events are becoming a major concern for resource management and public safety.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">"What defines a 'typical wildfire' in the West is changing. In the past, fires were often contained by natural barriers or managed by traditional practices. Today, the combination of climate change and human activity is leading to more extreme fire behavior, making suppression efforts significantly more challenging."</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">The number of large and very large fires on Forest Service land has been increasing over the past few decades. These fires, which burn over <span data-field="area_unit">{{ area_unit }}</span>, are often driven by prolonged drought and high temperatures.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">In some states in the increases in wildfires were driven more dramatically by <span data-field="driver_1">{{ driver_1 }}</span>, while in others, the primary driver was <span data-field="driver_2">{{ driver_2 }}</span>. The data suggests a complex interplay of climatic and land-use factors.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">On average, wildfires burn twice as much land area each year as they did in the 1970s. The data indicates a clear trend of increasing fire severity and extent across the region.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">The burn season in the U.S. is now longer than it was 40 years ago. Across the West, the first wildfire of the year starts earlier and the last one ends later, extending the period of high fire risk. This trend is projected to continue as climate change progresses.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">Previous research reveals that climatic changes, including increasing temperatures and changes in precipitation patterns, are contributing to the increased fire activity. These changes are interacting with land management practices, creating a feedback loop that exacerbates fire risk.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">U.S. Seasonal Drought Outlook</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">The U.S. Drought Monitor, released by the National Drought Mitigation Center, provides a snapshot of drought conditions across the country. The outlook for the coming months suggests a high probability of persistent drought conditions in the <span data-field="region_1">{{ region_1 }}</span> and <span data-field="region_2">{{ region_2 }}</span>.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6;">Drought severity is a critical factor in wildfire risk. Prolonged dry periods stress vegetation, making it more susceptible to ignition and rapid spread.</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Drought Severity Index:</p>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;">
          <div style="width: 45%; text-align: center;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Extreme</p>
            <div style="height: 10px; background-color: #ccc; margin-top: 5px;"><div style="width: 100%; height: 100%; background-color: red;"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div style="width: 45%; text-align: center;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Moderate</p>
            <div style="height: 10px; background-color: #ccc; margin-top: 5px;"><div style="width: 75%; height: 100%; background-color: orange;"></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 20px;">This map illustrates the projected drought conditions for the upcoming season.</p>
      <img src="placeholder_map.png" alt="Drought Map" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin-top: 10px;">
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

