        <h1 class="header-title">A Promising Method for Measuring OM/OC on IMPROVE Teflon Filters Using FT-IR</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Interagency Monitoring of Protected Visual Environments</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h2 class="section-title">Introduction</h2>
            <p>Organic material (OM) is a major contributor to fine particulate matter in urban and rural regions. Its accurate measurement is crucial for understanding air quality.</p>
            <p>This paper introduces a novel method utilizing Fourier Transform Infrared (FT-IR) spectroscopy for quantifying OM/OC on Teflon filters.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h2 class="section-title">Results</h2>
            <p>The results demonstrate the efficacy of the FT-IR method compared to traditional gravimetric analysis.</p>
            <p>The method provides high precision and sensitivity for measuring organic carbon fractions.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <h2 class="section-title">Methods</h2>
        <p>The FT-IR instrument was calibrated using certified reference materials. Samples were collected on Teflon filters and analyzed according to a standardized protocol.</p>
        <p>The spectral data was processed using chemometric techniques to extract OM and OC concentrations.</p>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Parameter</th>
                    <th>Measurement Technique</th>
                    <th>Notes</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
